---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="AI Integrations for Business Systems | Kelp Agency"
  description="Connect AI tools to the data and systems your team already uses, with practical workflows, permissions, and human oversight."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="AI Services"
    title="AI Integrations That Fit the Systems You Already Use"
    description="An AI tool is only helpful when it has the right information and a clear job. Kelp connects AI capabilities to the websites, stores, CRMs, catalogs, support tools, and internal systems your business already relies on. The goal is a workflow your team can trust, not another isolated dashboard."
    lottieFile="ai-integrations.json"
  />
  <section class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Teams often try an AI tool and then end up copying information in and
        out by hand. Customer details live in one system, product rules in
        another, and the AI response may be based on outdated or incomplete
        data. A promising demo turns into extra work when nobody has decided
        what the tool can read, what it can change, or what happens when a
        connection fails.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
      <p>
        We start with one useful task and map the systems behind it. Which
        source owns the information? How current does it need to be? Who can see
        it? What should happen when the tool is unsure? Those answers shape the
        integration, the interface, and the review process before we choose a
        model or build a connector.
      </p>
      <h2>Connect the Right Information</h2>
      <p>
        An integration might bring approved knowledge into a customer-facing
        assistant, use catalog data to help a shopper compare products,
        summarize a support issue for a team member, or route a qualified lead
        into a CRM. We can work with APIs, existing connectors, and custom
        middleware when the standard options cannot handle the workflow. The
        architecture depends on the data, permissions, and systems involved.
      </p>
      <h2>Plan for Real-World Exceptions</h2>
      <p>
        Data changes. Products are retired, customer records are incomplete, and
        external services occasionally fail. We plan how information is
        refreshed, how errors are surfaced, and when a person needs to take
        over. We also set boundaries around sensitive data and actions so the AI
        tool does not quietly make a decision it should only recommend.
      </p>
      <h2>Build Something Your Team Can Maintain</h2>
      <p>
        The integration should come with clear ownership: where content is
        updated, how access is managed, what is logged, and how the team checks
        quality over time. Kelp's broader{" "}
        <a href="/services/website-development/">
          website and application development work
        </a>{" "}
        helps connect the AI experience to the customer journey and the systems
        behind it.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use-case and system discovery</li>
        <li>Data flow, access, and permission planning</li>
        <li>API, connector, or middleware implementation</li>
        <li>Human review, error handling, and quality checks</li>
        <li>Documentation and an improvement plan after launch</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring us one task that takes too much manual effort or one customer
        interaction that breaks down because information is scattered. We can
        map the systems involved and recommend a focused first integration. Talk
        with Kelp about your workflow.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="h4">Do we need to replace our current software to add AI?</h3>
      <p>
        Usually the first step is to assess what your existing tools can provide
        through their APIs, exports, or approved connectors. We recommend a
        replacement only when the current system cannot support the job
        reliably.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
